# CQ-B1 — Which lawful bases permit processing of personal data?
# Probe (frozen CQ-B1): 6(1)(a-f) as a LegalBasis structure, NOT six controller obligations.
#
# Regime: (needs materialisation). The ABox types each basis with its specific subclass
# (e.g. `a gdprkg:LegalBasisConsent`); `?b a gdprkg:LegalBasis` matches only after the
# OWL 2 RL closure makes the inferred super-type explicit (see cq_sparql/README.md).
#
# Expected over art6.ttl: 6 rows — one per basis, each grounded in its 6(1) Point:
#   ex:basis-consent               -> ex:art6-p1-a
#   ex:basis-contract              -> ex:art6-p1-b
#   ex:basis-legal-obligation      -> ex:art6-p1-c
#   ex:basis-vital-interests       -> ex:art6-p1-d
#   ex:basis-public-task           -> ex:art6-p1-e
#   ex:basis-legitimate-interests  -> ex:art6-p1-f
PREFIX gdprkg: <https://w3id.org/gdprkg#>
SELECT ?basis ?point
WHERE {
  ?basis a gdprkg:LegalBasis ;
         gdprkg:groundedIn ?point .
}
ORDER BY ?point
